  - "Cybernetics: starts with none and avoids all augmentation like the plague - Mystics believe technology deadens the gift."
extraction_notes: |
  - Rifts Conversion Book One printed 107 (file p108), inside the Quorian entry. The page heads it "Quorian Oneiromancer O.C.C." and says it is identical to the Mystic O.C.C. "except with slightly different powers"; the survey calls it one of the section''s three R.C.C. pointers. It is an occupation limited to the Quorian (race_restrictions), with id and name carrying the race, and the id the `rifts-` prefix the batch-1 races use.
  - `copy_of: mystic` (RUE, the Rifts Mystic) records that everything but the powers is the Mystic''s: ladder, P.P.E., attribute requirements, bonuses, skills, money, equipment and restrictions are repeated in full because nothing composes one class from another, and regression asserts the two stay identical outside the except list.
  - The except list is what the page changes: psionics (Mind Block, Clairvoyance, Sixth Sense and Meditation plus four Sensitive ONLY, then one power per level from Healing, Sensitive or Physical - the Mystic''s Super powers at 4 and 8 are replaced), magic (four spells from levels one or two, then two per level up to his own level - replacing the Mystic''s 8/4/3/2 ladder), and the two natural abilities that describe those, plus the Chant of Dreaming. race_restrictions is the Quorian limit, which the Mystic does not carry.
  - The Chant of Dreaming is a spell row (level 0, 20 P.P.E., granted by name in magic.spells), the shape Wormwood''s class-specific powers take. Its success ratio is in the row''s description.
  - The Mystic''s O.C.C. notes are the Mystic''s and stand as that row states them.
